WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.334
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"the tonight show," everybody.

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.801
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:07.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:12.300
Well, guys this weekend was
Easter, Passover, and Ramadan.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.934
It's what's known
in the religious community

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:16.667
as a Holy Turducken.

00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.334
I do love Easter Sunday, though.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:20.767
It's the day parents give
their kids a basket of candy

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:22.400
then tell them
to sit quietly at church.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.167
It's just very interesting.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.467
Speaking of Easter,
today the Bidens hosted

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.334
the first White House
Easter Egg Roll

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:29.834
since the pandemic began,

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:34.534
and it was a huge event with
30,000 people in attendance.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:37.067
Yep, after two minutes
of rolling eggs across the lawn,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.267
the kids were like,
"Wow, I actually miss Zoom."

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:42.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.901
Meanwhile,
I was thrilled to be invited

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.100
and attend this year's
Easter Egg Roll.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.200
I did. I was there.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:51.100
Today. This morning.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.934
I told President Biden
it was an honor

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.300
and a privilege to be there.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.634
And he said, "Uh, Jimmy,
we invited 30,000 people."

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:58.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:01.334
But I did actually get to go
to the White House today.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.000
Yeah.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.167
When they said, "The President
wants to see you,"

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.367
I thought, "Damn, how bad
did I screw up my taxes?"

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.968
But I had an absolute blast.

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:14.234
Plus, good news --
during the egg hunt,

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.934
I found Trump's missing
call logs from January 6th.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:20.300
[ Applause ]

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.067
I found them.

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.367
[ Applause ]

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.267
I really did have the best time.

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.434
Do we have a photo of me
with the President?

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:31.834
Yeah, unbelievable.
It was great.

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:35.000
Actually, I read my book
"Nana Loves You More"

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.734
to all the kids.

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.567
Yeah, and --
[ cheers and applause ]

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:42.167
With the President and
the First Lady right next to me.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.334
This is a real photo.
This is from this morning. Yeah.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:45.767
[ Audience awws ]
Yeah.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.334
While I was reading to the kids,
the First Lady was so sweet.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.567
She was like, "Sound it out,
Jimmy. You can do it."

00:01:51.567 --> 00:01:53.601
Meanwhile,
I saw that, for Easter,

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:57.868
a photo of some knockoff
dollar-store Peeps went viral.

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.367
So it's dollar-store Peeps.

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.567
Take a look at these things,
this photo.

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:03.501
Wow.
-Oh.

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:08.834
-Looks like Peeps that appeared
in an episode of "Botched."

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:13.567
Looks like "The Real Housewives
of Marshmallowy Hills."

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:14.901
Let's switch gears.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:17.200
As you hopefully already know,
today is tax day.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.634
That's right. It's tax day.
Did you know that?

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:21.901
[ Scattered reaction ]

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.501
Alright. It was kind of
a non-reaction, though.

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.267
Like, "Yeah, uh, okay."

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:28.934
Yeah, it is tax day,
it's a pandemic, it's spring.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.067
So you can get taxed,
vaxed, and waxed.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.968
You can tell it's tax day
'cause right now

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.601
every billionaire
is laying low in space.

00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:40.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:41.968
Well, ahead of
today's tax deadline,

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:44.267
the White House released
the Bidens' tax return,

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.767
and together
they earned over $600,000.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.067
Making Joe Biden

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.767
the Jeff Bezos
of Wilmington, Delaware.

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:55.234
Yep, the President made money
from his salary, his book sales,

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:58.834
and his upcoming cameo
in "Magic Mike 3."

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:00.667
Well, according
to their tax return,

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:04.467
the Bidens did not receive
a refund this year.

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:07.334
When he saw, even Biden
was like, "Friggin' Biden."

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.634
[ Applause ]

00:03:13.634 --> 00:03:15.267
"Unbelievable."

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.033
Well, this is cool --
the FDA just authorized

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.968
the first-ever
COVID breath test.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.667
And it's more than 90%
effective.

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.801
Check out what this
breathalyzer looks like.

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.701
This is real. Yeah.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:29.801
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.267
-It's amazing.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.801
The guy combined luggage
with a Capri Sun.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.300
Ah, it's amazing.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.601
Now there's nasal swabs
and breathalyzers,

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.834
which means pretty soon
you'll see two lines at CVS,

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:43.067
one that says, "Up Yours,"
the other one says, "Blow Me."

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:45.167
-Hey! Whoa!

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:46.701
♪♪

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.100
Whoa. Whoa!

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.567
[ Applause ]

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.067
Whoa!

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:53.334
-Well, here in New York,
today former mayor

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:55.167
Michael Bloomberg
spoke at City Hall,

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.934
and people were saying
that his mask

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:59.334
seemed too tight for his face.

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:00.667
Look at this.

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:02.934
-But, seriously,
I was glad to have the chance

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.367
to welcome back each of
my predecessors to City Hall,

00:04:05.367 --> 00:04:07.734
and I'm glad that you're
carrying on that tradition.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.200
-You can see his lips.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.467
He spoke for about 10 more
seconds then passed out.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:17.000
Can we see that again? Yeah.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.601
It's, like, in his mouth.

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.167
[ Mumbling ]

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.601
Who makes his mask?
Lululemon makes his mask.

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:27.834
-Oh, boy.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.167
-You know that under that mask,

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.734
he looked like
a dollar-store Peep.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:32.501
Yeah...

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.367
[ Muffled shouting ]

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:39.300
[ Applause ]

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.901
Well, guys, right now it is time

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:43.300
for our latest installment
of "Tonight Show Polls."

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.501
Here. Check these out.

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:48.534
-♪ "Tonight Show" Polls ♪

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:50.667
[ Applause ]

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.334
-This first poll asked...

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.834
[ Applause ]

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.934
This next poll asked...

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.667
"Sure."

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.200
This next poll asked...

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.801
[ Applause ]

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.968
And, finally,
this last one asked...

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:56.067
That's all the time we have
for "Tonight Show Polls."

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.634
We have a great show tonight.

